  "settings": "Settings",
  "help": "Help",
  "helpScreenMessageAboutTitle": "About",
  "helpScreenMessageAboutContent": "This application allows you to record audio from a microphone or USB audio interface (your device must support USB OTG technology) to one of several tracks. You can set the audio codec, sample rate, bit rate, audio mode, auto gain, echo cancellation and noise suppression. You can also import an existing audio file.\n\nRecordings can be played synchronously or asynchronously, in a loop or not.\n\nIndividual tracks have the ability to set the speed, volume and start point, and export the recording.\n\nRecordings and their settings, as well as the graphic mode and language, are remembered after the application is closed.\n\nClick app logo on main screen to see recording settings.",
  "helpScreenMessageUsageTitle": "Using the app",
  "helpScreenMessageUsageContent": "Short press a colored track block or use a hotkey to perform one of the available actions.\n\nHold the track block or use the hotkey with the [Control] key to open the track details, which contains additional settings.\n\nThe hotkey is visible at the top of the track. You can also change it in the track details view.",
  "helpScreenMessageTrackActions": "Available actions legend",
  "helpScreenMessageTrackActions_state_empty": "start recording for track",
  "helpScreenMessageTrackActions_state_recording": "stop recording for track",
  "helpScreenMessageTrackActions_state_stopped": "start playing for track",
  "helpScreenMessageTrackActions_state_playing": "stop playing for track",
  "helpScreenMessageTrackActions_state_paused": "unpause playing for track",
  "helpScreenRecordingCodecsInfoTitle": "Audio recording codecs",
  "helpScreenRecordingCodecsInfoContent": "- MPEG-4 AAC LC (Advanced Audio Codec - Low Complexity) - Lossy compression, but better quality than MP3 at the same bitrate. Great for music and video.\n- MPEG-4 AAC ELD (Advanced Audio Codec - Enhanced Low Delay) - Optimized for very low latency. Lower quality than AAC LC, but better for live communication.\n- MPEG-4 AAC HE (Advanced Audio Codec - High Efficiency) - Designed for low bitrates (e.g. 32-64 kbps). Used for radio broadcasts and streaming. Higher latency compared to AAC LC.\n- WAV (Waveform Audio) - Lossless audio format, uses no compression. Very large files, but excellent quality. Perfect for professional editing and recording.\n- FLAC (Free Lossless Audio Codec) - Lossless, but compressed (about 50-70% less than WAV). Supports metadata, which WAV cannot. Great for archiving high-quality music.",
  "helpScreenRecordingCodecsChooseTitle": "Which codec to choose?",
  "helpScreenRecordingCodecsChooseContent": "\uD83D\uDCCC Which codec to choose?\n\uD83C\uDFA4 High quality recording → WAV or FLAC\n\uD83C\uDFB5 Good quality music at low bitrates → AAC LC\n\uD83D\uDCDE Real-time voice communication → AAC ELD\n\uD83D\uDCE1 Internet radio and streaming at low bitrates → AAC HE\n\uD83C\uDFA7 Audiophile music collection → FLAC",
